The thesis result tables in this directory, parity/golden/, and in its
subdirectories are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal
(CC0-1.0), by decision of their author, Marc Prinzing, on 2026-10-27
(MAR-94). To the extent possible under law, he waives all copyright and
related or neighbouring rights to them.

Legal code: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

Files covered:

- full_optimization_results.csv.gz, benchmarking_kpis.csv.gz: the thesis
  optimisation results and KPI table (gzipped copies of the thesis files);
- thesis_cluster_assignments.json, noise_digests.json: derived from the
  thesis code (MAR-12, MAR-10);
- golden_objectives.csv, golden_objectives.json: the objective values
  derived from the thesis tables and the thesis code (MAR-68);
- simulation_sweeps/: the thesis noise-level and asset-count sweep results,
  regenerated by running the thesis code (MAR-70).

Not covered:

- the parity fixture, parity/tests/data/thesis_eventset/, which is derived
  from the IRIS event set and recorded as CC-BY-4.0 (owner decision,
  MAR-94; docs/data-sources.md);
- the code under parity/, which is BSD-3-Clause (parity/LICENSE).

CC0 requires no attribution. Scientific practice still asks for it: please
cite the thesis repository (https://github.com/marc272/parametric-insurance-framework)
and the IRIS event set the results were computed from: Sparks, N. and
Toumi, R. (2024). The Imperial College Storm Model (IRIS) Dataset.
Scientific Data 11, 424, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-024-03250-y; data:
https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.c.6724251.v1.
